      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Mycobacterium gordonae is a slow growing, pigmented, non-tuberculous mycobacterium (NTM). It is commonly associated with environmental contamination of clinical specimens but it is also a recognized pathogen in immunocompromised hosts. We describe an immunocompetent child with a spontaneously occurring skin ulcer on the face caused by M. gordonae infection."},
